# Content-Security-Policy for the static deploy (Cloudflare Pages _headers).
#
# - script-src does NOT need 'unsafe-eval', and must not regain it. Nothing the
#   app bundles uses eval at all: the codec's deflate/inflate is `pako`, plain
#   ESM with no eval and no asm.js. Verified per build - `grep 'eval(' dist/`
#   over the emitted bundle finds nothing.
#
#   This line used to carry a much longer caveat, because the codec was backed
#   by `zlib-asm`, an asm.js port that shipped three eval sites (2016 Emscripten
#   runtime glue, none of them compression) and needed a local patch to strip
#   them so this policy could drop 'unsafe-eval'. That dependency and its patch
#   are gone; the constraint they were working around no longer exists. The
#   policy itself was verified live in Chrome under the zlib-asm build - the app
#   decoded and re-encoded all 9 builtin fixtures with zero
#   securitypolicyviolation events, while a deliberately injected inline
#   <script> WAS blocked - and pako is strictly less demanding than what passed.
# - img-src needs blob:: the preview PNG is shown via URL.createObjectURL(blob).
# - connect-src must include the preview Worker origin (the app's only outbound
#   call). Replace the placeholder with the deployed Worker origin.
# - style-src 'unsafe-inline' covers runtime-injected component styles.
# - script-src allows static.cloudflareinsights.com: Cloudflare AUTO-INJECTS its
#   Web Analytics beacon into proxied Pages responses, and the old policy blocked
#   it, so analytics silently recorded nothing and every page load logged two CSP
#   console errors (Lighthouse Best Practices 92 in production, 100 locally,
#   because nothing is injected on localhost).
#
#   The origin is listed WITHOUT a path on purpose. Cloudflare's docs suggest
#   `https://static.cloudflareinsights.com/beacon.min.js`, but the injected URL
#   carries a version segment (.../beacon.min.js/v4513226cd...), and a CSP source
#   with a path that does not end in `/` must match the path EXACTLY - so the
#   documented value would not match the thing actually being loaded, and would
#   break again on every beacon version bump.
#
#   No connect-src entry is needed. Under automatic injection the beacon reports
#   to this site's own /cdn-cgi/rum, which 'self' already covers; the separate
#   cloudflareinsights.com endpoint applies only to manual embedding.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; connect-src 'self' https://fmw-preview.wormeyman.workers.dev; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; script-src 'self' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com

# /version.json carries the git build stamp and exists to answer "did my deploy
# land?" (`pnpm run verify:deploy`). A cached copy would answer that question
# about the PREVIOUS deploy while looking authoritative, which is worse than no
# answer at all - so it is the one path here that must never be served stale.
#
# Unlike the hashed bundles, its URL is CONSTANT across deploys, so the edge has
# no cache key change to notice; `no-store` is what stops it being reused. The
# checker also sends a unique query string and `cache: no-store`, but belt and
# braces is deliberate: the browser tab a human opens to eyeball the file sends
# neither.
#
# This rule sets no Content-Security-Policy, so the `/*` policy above still
# applies to this path unchanged. Nothing here weakens it.
/version.json
  Cache-Control: no-store
